WEBVTT

00:00:01.656 --> 00:00:06.231
STICKS turns a threat-intelligence campaign into a plan that can be executed.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.269
This is the local workbench from the public repository.

00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:15.806
Campaign C0045, ShadowRay, is selected, with explicit search bounds.

00:00:19.848 --> 00:00:22.823
Enumerate realizations computes the plans offline.

00:00:23.098 --> 00:00:28.535
Sixty-four complete realizations share one procedure assignment and one causal structure.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.110
The search stopped at its ceiling of sixty-four, so other orders may remain.

00:00:37.175 --> 00:00:39.900
The causal graph draws one realization,

00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:43.050
from the initial state through each step to the goal.

00:00:43.312 --> 00:00:47.612
Each edge is a fact that one step produces and a later step consumes.

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:53.054
Select step two, T1190.

00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:56.029
It consumes two facts from the initial state:

00:00:56.329 --> 00:01:00.392
a reachable Ray dashboard and an available HTTP service.

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:05.029
It enables shell access on the target, which steps three to ten consume.

00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:10.868
Changing the execution order keeps the same graph.

00:01:11.131 --> 00:01:16.793
Only the numbers on the steps change: order six runs step ten before steps nine and eight.

00:01:21.329 --> 00:01:26.379
Download JSON saves the inputs and the result, and the command shown recomputes it.

00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:30.491
The operational status is not run: planning executes nothing.

00:01:31.961 --> 00:01:34.761
Execution is a separate laboratory workflow.

00:01:36.005 --> 00:01:40.630
Here is an edited capture of an earlier fresh C0026 run.

00:01:41.312 --> 00:01:44.075
The artifact starts three virtual machines.

00:01:44.752 --> 00:01:49.602
One hosts Caldera, one represents the attacker, and one is the Linux target.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.985
After enrollment, Caldera dispatches the target actions.

00:01:55.672 --> 00:02:00.185
The runtime records five observed occurrences and one simulated occurrence.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.547
No occurrence failed or was blocked.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.370
An independent probe checks the target after execution.

00:02:09.993 --> 00:02:16.155
It verifies that the collected material matches the declared sources and that the chunks reconstruct the archive.

00:02:18.642 --> 00:02:22.892
Finally, the runner destroys the virtual machines and seals the receipt.

00:02:24.072 --> 00:02:26.747
The artifact validator returned exit zero.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.950
Check that all three virtual machines are gone.
